{"tree":[{"name":"README.md","type":"file","content":"# notes-app\n\nA minimal command-line notes manager written in Python. Supports creating, listing, searching, and deleting notes. Intended as a small learning project.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3.10 or higher\n- pytest (for running tests)\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/tariq-dev/notes-app.git\ncd notes-app\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom src.notes import save_note, list_notes, search_notes, delete_note\n\n# Save a note\nsave_note(title=\"Shopping list\", body=\"milk, eggs, bread\")\n\n# List all notes\nnotes = list_notes()\nprint(notes)\n\n# Search by title\nresults = search_notes(\"shopping\")\nprint(results)\n\n# Delete a note by ID\ndelete_note(1)\n```\n\n## Running tests\n\n```bash\npytest tests/\n```\n\nAll tests should pass before you open a pull request.\n\n## Project structure\n\n```\nnotes-app/\n├── src/\n│   └── notes.py        # core notes logic\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_notes.py   # regression tests\n├── requirements.txt\n├── README.md\n└── CONTRIBUTING.md\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) before opening a pull request.\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n"},{"name":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"file","content":"# Contributing to notes-app\n\nThanks for your interest in contributing. This is a small project — contributions are welcome, but please read this first.\n\n## Before you start\n\n- Check the open issues. If you want to work on one, **leave a comment on the issue first** and wait for a response. This avoids two people working on the same thing.\n- If you find a new bug, open an issue before submitting a PR. Describe the bug, steps to reproduce, and the Python version you're using.\n- One issue per PR. Don't bundle multiple fixes into one pull request.\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/tariq-dev/notes-app.git\ncd notes-app\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Running tests\n\n```bash\npytest tests/\n```\n\nAll tests must pass before you open a PR. If you're fixing a bug, add a test that fails on the buggy code and passes after your fix.\n\n## Branch naming\n\nUse this format:\n\n```\nfix/issue-<number>-short-description\nfeat/short-description\ndocs/short-description\n```\n\nExamples:\n- `fix/issue-12-empty-title-validation`\n- `docs/update-readme-usage`\n\n## Opening a pull request\n\n- Link the issue your PR fixes using `Fixes #<issue-number>` in the PR description.\n- Keep the PR small. A focused change is easier to review and faster to merge.\n- Describe what you changed and why — not just what files you touched.\n- Don't ping the maintainer repeatedly. Reviews happen within a week or so.\n\n## Code style\n\n- Follow the existing style in `notes.py` — no external formatters required.\n- Add docstrings to any new functions.\n- Keep functions small and focused.\n\n## What counts as a contribution\n\n- Bug fixes with tests\n- Documentation improvements\n- Clearer error messages\n\n**What we won't merge:**\n- Whitespace-only changes\n- Reformatting without functional changes\n- AI-generated code that the contributor hasn't read, tested, or understood\n"},{"name":"requirements.txt","type":"file","content":"pytest==8.3.3\n"},{"name":"src","type":"dir","children":[{"name":"notes.py","type":"file","content":"# notes.py — v1.0.0\n# A simple in-memory notes manager.\n# Supports creating, listing, searching, and deleting notes.\n\n_notes = {}\n_next_id = 1\n\n\ndef save_note(title, body=\"\"):\n    \"\"\"Save a new note with a title and optional body.\n\n    Returns a dict with 'status' and 'id' on success,\n    or 'error' on failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    global _next_id\n\n    # BUG 1: No check for empty title after stripping whitespace.\n    # If title is \"\" or \"   \", clean_title will be \"\" and the note\n    # is saved with a blank title. No error is raised.\n    clean_title = title.strip()\n\n    note = {\n        \"id\": _next_id,\n        \"title\": clean_title,\n        \"body\": body,\n    }\n    _notes[_next_id] = note\n    _next_id += 1\n    return {\"status\": \"saved\", \"id\": note[\"id\"]}\n\n\ndef delete_note(note_id):\n    \"\"\"Delete a note by its integer ID.\n\n    Returns a dict with 'status' on success,\n    or raises KeyError if the ID does not exist.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BUG 2: No check whether note_id exists before deleting.\n    # If the caller passes an ID that was already deleted or never existed,\n    # this raises an unhandled KeyError instead of returning a clean error.\n    del _notes[note_id]\n    return {\"status\": \"deleted\"}\n\n\ndef search_notes(query):\n    \"\"\"Search notes by title.\n\n    Returns a list of notes whose title contains the query string.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for note in _notes.values():\n        # BUG 3: Case-sensitive comparison.\n        # search_notes(\"shopping\") will not find a note titled \"Shopping List\".\n        # Fix is to compare both strings lowercased.\n        if query in note[\"title\"]:\n            results.append(note)\n    return results\n\n\ndef list_notes():\n    \"\"\"Return all saved notes as a list.\"\"\"\n    # BUG 4: Returns a direct reference to the internal dict's values view\n    # converted to a list — but each note dict inside is still the live object.\n    # A caller who does list_notes()[0][\"title\"] = \"hacked\" will silently\n    # corrupt the internal store.\n    return list(_notes.values())\n\n\ndef get_note(note_id):\n    \"\"\"Return a single note by ID, or None if it does not exist.\"\"\"\n    return _notes.get(note_id)\n\n\ndef clear_all():\n    \"\"\"Remove all notes. Used in tests to reset state between runs.\"\"\"\n    global _next_id\n    _notes.clear()\n    _next_id = 1\n"}]},{"name":"tests","type":"dir","children":[{"name":"test_notes.py","type":"file","content":"\"\"\"\nRegression tests for notes-app.\n\nEach test class covers one bug. Within each class:\n- test_buggy_*  shows the wrong behavior in v1.0.0\n- test_fixed_*  shows the correct behavior in v1.1.0\n\nThese tests are the source of truth for the scenario JSON.\nIf they pass, verifiedByTest can be set to true in issues.json.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport os\n\n# Make sure both src modules are importable\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\"))\n\nimport pytest\nfrom src.notes import (\n    save_note, delete_note, search_notes, list_notes, clear_all\n)\nfrom src.notes_fixed import (\n    save_note as save_note_fixed,\n    delete_note as delete_note_fixed,\n    search_notes as search_notes_fixed,\n    list_notes as list_notes_fixed,\n    clear_all as clear_all_fixed,\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Reset state before every test so tests don't bleed into each other\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\ndef reset_state():\n    clear_all()\n    clear_all_fixed()\n    yield\n    clear_all()\n    clear_all_fixed()\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Bug 1 — Empty title is saved silently (no validation)\n# Lesson: genuine_good_pick  |  regressionTestId: notes-app/empty-title-crash\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass TestEmptyTitle:\n\n    def test_buggy_empty_title_saves_silently(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: saving with an empty title succeeds — wrong behavior.\"\"\"\n        result = save_note(title=\"\", body=\"some content\")\n        # Bug: no error returned, note is saved with blank title\n        assert result.get(\"status\") == \"saved\"\n        assert result.get(\"error\") is None\n\n    def test_buggy_whitespace_only_title_saves_silently(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: whitespace-only title also saves silently.\"\"\"\n        result = save_note(title=\"   \", body=\"some content\")\n        assert result.get(\"status\") == \"saved\"\n\n    def test_fixed_empty_title_returns_error(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: empty title returns a validation error.\"\"\"\n        result = save_note_fixed(title=\"\", body=\"some content\")\n        assert result.get(\"error\") == \"Title cannot be empty.\"\n        assert result.get(\"status\") is None\n\n    def test_fixed_whitespace_only_title_returns_error(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: whitespace-only title also returns a validation error.\"\"\"\n        result = save_note_fixed(title=\"   \", body=\"some content\")\n        assert result.get(\"error\") == \"Title cannot be empty.\"\n\n    def test_fixed_valid_title_saves_successfully(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: a valid title saves correctly.\"\"\"\n        result = save_note_fixed(title=\"Shopping list\", body=\"milk, eggs\")\n        assert result.get(\"status\") == \"saved\"\n        assert \"id\" in result\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Bug 2 — Delete crashes with KeyError on invalid ID\n# Lesson: claimed_never_started  |  regressionTestId: notes-app/delete-keyerror\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass TestDeleteInvalidId:\n\n    def test_buggy_delete_nonexistent_raises_keyerror(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: deleting a non-existent ID raises KeyError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(KeyError):\n            delete_note(999)\n\n    def test_buggy_delete_already_deleted_raises_keyerror(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: deleting an already-deleted note raises KeyError.\"\"\"\n        save_note(title=\"Temp note\")\n        delete_note(1)\n        with pytest.raises(KeyError):\n            delete_note(1)  # second delete crashes\n\n    def test_fixed_delete_nonexistent_returns_error(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: deleting a non-existent ID returns a clean error dict.\"\"\"\n        result = delete_note_fixed(999)\n        assert result.get(\"error\") == \"Note with id 999 does not exist.\"\n\n    def test_fixed_delete_valid_id_succeeds(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: deleting a valid ID works correctly.\"\"\"\n        save_note_fixed(title=\"Temp note\")\n        result = delete_note_fixed(1)\n        assert result.get(\"status\") == \"deleted\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Bug 3 — Search is case-sensitive\n# Lesson: good_first_issue_hard  |  regressionTestId: notes-app/search-case-sensitive\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass TestCaseSensitiveSearch:\n\n    def test_buggy_search_misses_different_case(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: searching 'shopping' does not find 'Shopping List'.\"\"\"\n        save_note(title=\"Shopping List\", body=\"milk, eggs\")\n        results = search_notes(\"shopping\")\n        # Bug: returns empty list because comparison is case-sensitive\n        assert results == []\n\n    def test_buggy_search_only_finds_exact_case(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: only exact case match works.\"\"\"\n        save_note(title=\"Shopping List\", body=\"milk, eggs\")\n        results = search_notes(\"Shopping\")\n        assert len(results) == 1\n\n    def test_fixed_search_is_case_insensitive(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: searching 'shopping' correctly finds 'Shopping List'.\"\"\"\n        save_note_fixed(title=\"Shopping List\", body=\"milk, eggs\")\n        results = search_notes_fixed(\"shopping\")\n        assert len(results) == 1\n        assert results[0][\"title\"] == \"Shopping List\"\n\n    def test_fixed_search_uppercase_query(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: uppercase query also finds lowercase titles.\"\"\"\n        save_note_fixed(title=\"meeting notes\", body=\"discussed roadmap\")\n        results = search_notes_fixed(\"MEETING\")\n        assert len(results) == 1\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Bug 4 — list_notes returns mutable internal state\n# Lesson: no_reproduction_steps  |  regressionTestId: notes-app/mutable-list\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass TestMutableListReturn:\n\n    def test_buggy_caller_can_corrupt_internal_state(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.0.0: mutating a note from list_notes corrupts the store.\"\"\"\n        save_note(title=\"Original title\", body=\"body\")\n        notes = list_notes()\n        # Mutate the returned object\n        notes[0][\"title\"] = \"Corrupted\"\n        # The internal store is now corrupted\n        from src.notes import get_note\n        stored = get_note(1)\n        assert stored[\"title\"] == \"Corrupted\"  # bug: internal state changed\n\n    def test_fixed_caller_cannot_corrupt_internal_state(self):\n        \"\"\"v1.1.0: mutating a note from list_notes does not affect the store.\"\"\"\n        save_note_fixed(title=\"Original title\", body=\"body\")\n        notes = list_notes_fixed()\n        notes[0][\"title\"] = \"Attempted corruption\"\n        from src.notes_fixed import get_note as get_note_fixed\n        stored = get_note_fixed(1)\n        assert stored[\"title\"] == \"Original title\"  # fix: internal state safe\n"}]}]}